     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the usual maximum single dose is about 1,000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** That is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals.** That is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg twice daily.** This is a typical starting or titration dose.\n- **Another dose.** If 1700 mg was intentional, for example a daily total split differently, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
